<article class="article-layout">
    <header class="post-hero">
        <div class="post-hero-inner">
            <h1>Welcome to Grove</h1>
            <time datetime="2026-04-14">14.04.2026</time>
        </div>
    </header>
    <div class="post-body">
        <p>Grove takes your leaf posts and assembles them into a site. Structure comes from your folder hierarchy. Collections let you curate sequences. The build pipeline generates static HTML that works without JavaScript.</p>
<h2>What you get</h2>
<ul>
<li>Real URLs derived from your content tree</li>
<li>RSS feeds (XML and JSON)</li>
<li>Open Graph tags on every page</li>
<li>Client-side search backed by IndexedDB</li>
<li>Dark mode with no flash</li>
<li>Offline support via service worker</li>
</ul>
<h2>Next steps</h2>
<p>Write a post, build, and see it rendered.</p>

    </div>
</article>
